================================================================================
3. Third-party material
================================================================================

The benchmark (data/code_doc_pairs.json) contains short Java code snippets
extracted from third-party open-source repositories. Copyright of those
snippets remains with their original authors and is governed by the license of
the corresponding upstream repository. The snippets are included here solely
for research and reproducibility purposes.

The Java formatter used to build code slices (`code/java_formatter/java_format.py`)
relies on the `astyle-py` package, which bundles a WebAssembly build of Artistic
Style. Both are MIT-licensed:

- Artistic Style — MIT License — https://astyle.sourceforge.net/
  (Copyright (c) 2018 Jim Pattee and contributors)
- astyle-py — MIT License — https://pypi.org/project/astyle-py/
  (Copyright (c) 2020 Ivan Grokhotkov; the bundled `libastyle.wasm` is built from
  Artistic Style, also MIT)

They are installed as ordinary Python dependencies (see `requirements.txt`); no
third-party source is vendored in this package.
